TA-authid
====

Collects identity-client state: name-service lookup order from /etc/nsswitch.conf, SSSD service state and configured domains, system Kerberos ticket cache count, and nscd/oddjob presence where installed. Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype authid:status) and authid.* metrics to index=metrics (sourcetype authid:metrics); local-auth-only hosts report the baseline without alarms.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * none - reads /etc/nsswitch.conf, systemctl, klist, sssctl when present
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="authid:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="authid:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="authid.*" by host
  | mstats avg("authid.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=authid:status  (nsswitch order, sssd state/domains, krb ticket count)
Metrics: authid.sssd_active, authid.krb_tickets, authid.nscd_active on index=metrics
Dashboards: TA-Authid > Authid Overview / Authid Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-authid/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * klist reads the system ticket cache only when a keytab/agent is present.
  * SSSD sections appear only when sssd is installed.

